# Build context for apps/api/Dockerfile (context = repository root).
#
# The Dockerfile's prune stage copies the whole context so `turbo prune` can
# read every workspace manifest, so this file is what keeps the context small
# and free of secrets. Never weaken the secrets section.

# --- Secrets: never enter any image layer, not even a discarded build stage ---
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.crt
**/*.der
**/.dev.vars
**/.npmrc

# --- VCS, CI and editor state ---
.git
.github
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store

# --- Dependencies and build output (rebuilt inside the image) ---
**/node_modules
**/.pnpm-store
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/.cache
**/dist
**/out
**/build
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.log
# Prisma client: regenerated in the image from schema.prisma.
packages/db/generated

# --- Native/desktop artifacts ---
apps/desktop/src-tauri/target
apps/desktop/src-tauri/binaries
apps/mcp/.wrangler
**/*.dmg
**/*.AppImage
**/*.deb

# --- Not part of any build (workspace manifests stay: turbo prune needs them) ---
apps/intro-video/**
!apps/intro-video/package.json
docs
packaging
tasks
.sisyphus
.omo
.omx
.opencode-monitor
ISSUES.md
logo.png
logo.jpg
logo-trimmed.png
test-apply-patch.js
test-edit.js
